{"created": "2025-03-11T20:44:10.891241+00:00", "modified": "2025-03-12T14:17:12.111322+00:00", "id": 15008561, "conceptrecid": "15008560", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15008561", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.15008560", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15008561", "metadata": {"title": "Distributed Acoustic Sensing fin whale labeled dataset for level estimations", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15008561", "publication_date": "2025-03-11", "description": "<h2>Overview</h2>\n<p>This dataset aims to support the work presented in</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Link to JASA-EL paper</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It contains recordings from three locations across the North Pacific Ocean (OOI South; &nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org//10.1121/10.0017104\">Wilcock et al. (2023)</a> and <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.58046/5J60-FJ89\">Wilcock and Ocean Observatories Initiative (2023)</a>), North Atlantic Ocean (Svalbard; &nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmars.2023.1130898\">R&oslash;rstadbotnen et al. (2023)</a>; <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.18710/Q8OSON\">R&oslash;rstadbotnen and Landr&oslash; (2023)</a>), and Mediterranean Sea (MedSea; &nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1121/10.0004129\">Rivet et al. (2021)</a>), each with a unique DAS configuration with variability in depth range, seafloor sediments, length of the instrumented fiber, and gauge length. They all contain recordings of fin whale 20 Hz calls.<br><br>The python repository developed to analyze this dataset <a href=\"https://github.com/DAS4Whales/DAS_levels\">DAS_Levels</a> is available on GitHub and citable.</p>\n<h2>Dataset characteristics</h2>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Parameter</strong></th>\n<th><strong>OOI South</strong></th>\n<th><strong>MedSea</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Svalbard</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Location</strong></td>\n<td>Pacific City (OR), USA</td>\n<td>Toulon, France</td>\n<td>Longyearbyen, Norway</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ocean</strong></td>\n<td>North East Pacific Ocean</td>\n<td>Mediterranean Sea</td>\n<td>North Atlantic Ocean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Interrogator</strong></td>\n<td>OptaSense QuantX</td>\n<td>Alcatel OptoDAS</td>\n<td>Alcatel OptoDAS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DAS Coverage (km)</strong></td>\n<td>97.0</td>\n<td>52.0</td>\n<td>137.9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gauge Length (m)</strong></td>\n<td>51.0</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sampling Frequency (Hz)</strong></td>\n<td>200</td>\n<td>72.7</td>\n<td>625</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Channel Spacing (m)</strong></td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sediment Types</strong></td>\n<td>Sand/Mud (<a href=\"https://data.shom.fr/\">source</a>)</td>\n<td>Sand/Mud (<a href=\"https://data.shom.fr/\" target=\"_new\">source</a>)</td>\n<td>Sludge (<a href=\"https://www.ngu.no/en/geologiske-kart\" target=\"_new\">source </a>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Date</strong></td>\n<td>20211102-190014UTC</td>\n<td>20230922-091304UTC</td>\n<td>20220822-123957UTC</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Whale Apex (km)</strong></td>\n<td>31.95</td>\n<td>35.35</td>\n<td>79.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Whale Offset (m)</strong></td>\n<td>340</td>\n<td>2375</td>\n<td>1500</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>Folder structure</h2>\n<p>The main folder contains the csv `dataset_config.csv` useful for file associations and path management.</p>\n<p>Each sub folder contains:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>`DASPosition/`, with position file for the DAS cable including Lat, Lon, Depth</li>\n<li>`annotations/`, with a label csv file containing whale apex, offset and timing</li>\n<li>`data/`, with the signal and noise data</li>\n<li>`readme.txt` containing detailed informations about the dataset</li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Bouffaut, L\u00e9a", "affiliation": "Cornell University", "orcid": "0000-0002-5318-294X"}, {"name": "Goestchel, Quentin", "affiliation": "University of Washington", "orcid": "0000-0003-2895-1089"}, {"name": "Sladen, Anthony", "affiliation": "CNRS", "orcid": "0000-0003-4126-0020"}, {"name": "Hartog, Arthur", "affiliation": "Fosina", "orcid": "0000-0001-6930-4561"}, {"name": "Klinck, Holger", "affiliation": "Cornell University", "orcid": "0000-0003-1078-7268"}], "keywords": ["distributed acoustic sensing", "acoustic levels", "bioacoustics", "fin whale"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.18710/Q8OSON", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.58046/5J60-FJ89", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1121/10.0004129", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.0.0", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15008957", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "15008560"}}]}}, "title": "Distributed Acoustic Sensing fin whale labeled dataset for level estimations", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15008561", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15008561", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15008561?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15008561", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15008561", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15008561", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15008561/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15008560", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15008560", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15008560", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15008560", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:15008561/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:15008561/sequence